From b023299dfdbb04ff8a4da6d0ceced4ecc7bd3c74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GrgaPalcic <26028466+GrgaPalcic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:30:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: a sharded share resume adopts only when the
 untwinned tail pays (TF_GLM_KV_SHARE_UNTWINNED_PCT)

A resumed pass under the share takes no twin and prefills at about 75 % of the twinned rate (measured: about 1,310 against 1,750 tok/s). A kept prefix is adopted only when the new tokens are at most 3x the prefix at the default 75; kv_shard_resumes_skipped_total counts the passes that ran cold instead.
---
 zig/src/core/lanes/kv_parts.zig               |  2 +
 zig/src/families/glm/cuda_kv_shard.zig        |  1 +
 .../families/glm/cuda_kv_shard_pages_test.zig | 97 +++++++++++++++++++
 zig/src/families/glm/cuda_lanes.zig           |  1 +
 zig/src/families/glm/cuda_ranks.zig           |  6 ++
 zig/src/families/glm/cuda_ranks_test.zig      | 23 +++++
 zig/src/families/glm/cuda_share.zig           | 65 +++++++++++++
 7 files changed, 195 insertions(+)

